# Repository text normalisation.
#
# Windows checkouts used to come back CRLF because the host had
# core.autocrlf=true and no attributes file. That silently broke
# exact-text edits, `grep`-style searches for `\n`, and any tool that
# compares checked-out bytes to repository bytes: the "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" warning was the only symptom.
#
# Pin LF for text in both the index and the worktree so a clone behaves
# the same on Windows, macOS and Linux.
* text=auto eol=lf

# cmd.exe is the one consumer that still wants CRLF.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary artifacts must never be normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.exe binary
*.dll binary
*.lib binary
*.pdb binary
*.rlib binary

# Generated evidence and local tool state are never committed.
wat/evidence/** -text
